+# Slice 1 plan: the new board (spec v4)
+
+*Integrator's plan, 2026-11-18, written on autopilot (the user is away and asked for the slices to be built without stopping; `verbatim_prompt_log/bundle_21/user_requested_documents/02_autopilot_decisions.md` logs every choice made without them). The specification is `verbatim_prompt_log/bundle_21/user_requested_documents/01_spec_v4.md`; clause IDs below refer to it.*
+
+**Slice 1 = ★D8 (a) item 1:**
+- the new board: AXIOMS column, PROPOSITIONS canvas, the Vocabulary and Definitions columns above, user-drawn arrows, kinds by position, pending, "follows from nothing", glows and bands, and the A|P box;
+- **Formalize for dependencies** on today's run and review machinery (all-or-nothing Accept, today's checks plus the new arrow checks);
+- the Current view is read-only while a run is active, and Accept refuses when the files drifted (the user's third mid-turn message: ES-7, ES-9, UN-3).
+
+**Not in slice 1:**
+- the review list, arrow items, the session Undo stack (slice 2);
+- FROZEN and the freeze UI (slice 3);
+- the transform window (slice 4);
+- references (slice 5).
+
+Claude adds no arrows of its own in slice 1. Missing premises stay today's "Claude suggests" ghosts; adopting one ("I hold this") writes the card and its arrow, as today.
+
+---
+
+## 0. Rules for everyone working on slice 1
+
+The builder rules file (`/tmp/claude-1000/-home-zhengyew-telelean/20626c17-0334-4498-ad86-9dc24b7010ed/scratchpad/builder_rules.md`) is pasted into every builder's brief. In short:
+- no git changes;
+- no installs;
+- never real Claude (`TELELEAN_NO_REAL_CLAUDE=1`);
+- never write `packages/extension/dist` or `out`, because the user's installed extension runs from there;
+- one heavy job at a time, under the memory cap (`capped.sh`);
+- vitest with one worker.
+
+**Baseline before any change** (2026-11-18, this machine, under the cap):
+- `tsc --noEmit` is clean for core (test config), runner (test config), webview (both configs) and extension;
+- vitest: core 48 files and 500/500 tests, webview 8 files and 130/130, extension 21 files and 180/180, runner (see §9).
+
+**Test builds of the webview** go to a scratch folder: `TELELEAN_WEBVIEW_OUT=<dir> npx vite build`. The Playwright harness serves that folder when the same variable is set (`test/harness/serve.mjs`). Only the integrator runs the browser tests, and only when RAM allows (AP-6).
+
+## 1. Order of work (sub-slices; each ends compiling, with unit tests passing, and a patch saved)
+
+| Sub-slice | What | Main clauses |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1a | Two kinds: AXIOM and PROPOSITION (model, markup aliases, statuses `pending` and `established`, layout, planners, labels; the board shows two columns for now) | Terms, CF-2, CF-4, BD-6 (status part), BD-9, B.4–B.6 |
+| 1b | Arrows as board edits: draw, delete, follows from nothing, axiom → proposition by an arrow, proposition → axiom (Move to axioms), Mark pending; cycle refusal; arrow selection | AR-1–8, CF-4, CM-2 (arrows) |
+| 1c | The canvas and the columns above: pan, zoom, right-drag, the right-click menu, keyboard, placement and positions, arrows across both parts, the AXIOMS header counts | BD-1–4, CM-7 |
+| 1d | Glows and bands, arrow looks, legend | BD-5–7, BD-9 |
+| 1e | Formalize for dependencies: the Context Menu section replacing the tray, arrow selection as the question, the run without the premises write, the AR-8 dialog, the gate's no-hidden-edges check | ES-2 (single target), AR-8, CM-1–5, B.1–B.3 |
+| 1f | Read-only Current during a run; Accept refuses on drift; board Undo locked during a run | ES-7, ES-9, UN-3 |
+| 1g | End-to-end tests (Playwright, run one spec at a time against a scratch build) and the user guide for the new board; the VS Code suite type-checks | §6 |
+
+**One target per Formalize in slice 1 (AP-9).** If the selected arrows point into several propositions, the action is disabled with the reason "One target at a time for now: select arrows into one card." Several targets, proved sources first, come with the review list (slice 2), because today's run engine and review have exactly one target.
+
+## 2. Contracts (integrator's changes; builders implement them as written)
+
+### 2.1 core `model.ts`
+- `NodeType = 'AXIOM' | 'PROPOSITION'`, and `NODE_TYPES = ['AXIOM', 'PROPOSITION']`. `isNodeType` accepts only these.
+- New `parseNodeType(raw: string): { type: NodeType; alias?: 'ASSUMPTION' | 'DERIVATION' | 'GOAL' } | undefined`. It is case-insensitive, as today: lower case keeps TL019's hint. It maps ASSUMPTION → AXIOM, and DERIVATION and GOAL → PROPOSITION.
+- `ProofStatus`: `{ kind: 'pending' }` replaces `{ kind: 'pending-promotion' }`.
+- `StatusFlag` changes:
+  - remove `proved-goal` and `claimed`;
+  - rename `rests-on-claimed` to `rests-on-pending`;
+  - add `established` (B.5).
+- `TlNode`: add `fromNothing?: boolean`. It is true when the block has the field `follows_from: nothing` (AR-5, B.6).
+
+### 2.2 core markup
+- `type:` takes AXIOM or PROPOSITION. ASSUMPTION, DERIVATION and GOAL are read as aliases, with no diagnostic, and never rewritten.
+- telelean writes AXIOM or PROPOSITION only when it writes a `type:` line: for add-node, and for a kind change.
+- "Follows from nothing" is its own known field, `follows_from: nothing` (B.6, decided after the soundness review's S-12, AP-15). It goes in FIELD_ORDER right after `premises`.
+  - Any other value is a markup error (new code TL022, "follows_from takes only the value nothing"), and the field is then ignored.
+  - With non-empty `premises:` it is an error too (TL023, "a card cannot both follow from nothing and have arrows"); the arrows win and the mark is ignored.
+  - A `premises:` line with no valid id stays what it is today. It is never the mark.
+  - The field is data telelean keeps (CF-3): G5 compares it, so Claude cannot write it.
+- G5's byte comparison of the markup is unchanged.
+
+### 2.3 core `layout.ts`
+- `columns: { AXIOM: string[]; PROPOSITION: string[] }`. Old layouts are parsed leniently: ASSUMPTION → AXIOM, and DERIVATION + GOAL → PROPOSITION, concatenated.
+- Add `positions?: Record<string, { x: number; y: number }>`: canvas coordinates of propositions (1c).
+- Serialisation stays stable, as today.
+
+### 2.4 core `actions.ts` (BoardAction) and planners
+- `add-node` gains an optional `position` (1c).
+- `change-kind`:
+  - `to: 'AXIOM'` (proposition → axiom) removes the `premises:` line, as part of the same plan (AR-7). The `.holds` handling is D-11's old D→A / G→A row.
+  - `to: 'PROPOSITION'` is refused with `invalid`: "To make an axiom a proposition, draw an arrow into it, or mark it 'follows from nothing'." (AR-6)
+- New `{ kind: 'add-arrows'; target: string; sources: string[]; confirmed?: boolean }`.
+  - It adds the sources to the target's `premises:`, keeping the existing order and appending new ones; duplicates are ignored.
+  - It refuses, with `invalid` and a message naming the cycle or the problem:
+    - a cycle (over declared premises and verified proof edges);
+    - another subject;
+    - a self-arrow;
+    - an unknown id.
+  - It removes `fromNothing`.
+  - **Into an axiom:** the same plan also changes the target's kind to PROPOSITION, by D-11's old A→D row: the `.holds` axiom stays, now **pending**. When cards rest on it (`kindChangeImpact`), the planner answers `needs-confirmation`, with the text "N cards that rest on it will lose their green glow until it is proved", unless `confirmed`.
+- New `{ kind: 'remove-arrows'; arrows: { source: string; target: string }[]; confirmed?: boolean }`. It removes the entries. If the target's proof uses a removed source (a verified edge), it answers `needs-confirmation` (spec A16) unless `confirmed`.
+- New `{ kind: 'set-from-nothing'; id: string; on: boolean; confirmed?: boolean }`.
+  - `on` on a proposition with no premises writes `follows_from: nothing`; on a proposition with premises it is refused.
+  - `on` on an axiom also changes its kind to PROPOSITION, as add-arrows does, with the same confirmation.
+  - `off` removes the `follows_from` line.
+- New `{ kind: 'claim-pending'; id: string }` (AR-8, ★D7 (b)). It applies to a PROPOSITION with a Lean statement and no `.holds`, and adds `axiom n.holds : n` (D-11 `add-holds-axiom`). It is refused otherwise.
+- New `{ kind: 'move-cards'; positions: Record<string, { x: number; y: number }> }`. It is layout only, like `reorder`, and one Undo step labelled "Move: …".
+- `set-premises` stays in the type for old History entries, but nothing sends it any more (1e).
+- Each new action is one Undo step and one History entry.
+
+### 2.5 core `protocol.ts`
+- New webview → host messages, with hand-written validators as for the others: `addArrows`, `removeArrows`, `setFromNothing`, `claimPending`, `moveCards`.
+- `startRun` keeps `{ target, premises }`, but the host now checks two things. Every premise must be a declared arrow source into the target; with `premises: []`, the target must be marked "follows from nothing". Every premise must have a `.holds` (axiom or theorem). Refusal texts: "Select arrows into one card." and "‹card› is not proved: mark it pending first."
+
+### 2.6 runner
+- The run no longer writes `premises:` at its start (`manager.ts` ~L856): the arrows are already there (AR-4, ES-5).
+- Ghost adoption still appends the adopted card's id to the target's `premises:`: that is the arrow of "I hold this".
+- `gate/normalise.ts`: the GOAL→DERIVATION lifecycle item goes. The run's "Card changes" ticks disappear.
+- **New gate rule `undeclared-premise` (B.2).**
+  - At `gate-proved` (and `gate-other` when a target proof is present), compute direct(T): walk the facts' references from `T.holds` through declarations that belong to no card, up to the first card `.holds`. The board does the same in `core/src/project/edges.ts` `directUses`.
+  - Every card reached must be a selected premise, or an adopted ghost.
+  - Message: "The proof uses ‹sentence›, which is not one of the arrows you selected."
+- `prompts.ts`: the wording becomes arrows and "follows from nothing" instead of "These suffice" and "Self-evident?".
+- **1f: Accept with drift.** If the user's files changed since the run's base, Accept refuses: "Your files changed since this run started (‹files›). Undo those edits, or discard the run." The rebase path is no longer taken. It stays in the code, unreachable, until slice 2 removes it.
+
+### 2.7 extension host
+- `boardSession` routes the new messages.
+- While a run of the model folder is active (any state before Accept or Discard), every board edit is refused with "An edit session is active: the board can't be edited until you accept or discard it (ES-9)." This covers add, edit, delete, kind, arrows, from-nothing, claim-pending, moves, Undo, Redo and History revert.
+
+### 2.8 webview
+- Two kinds:
+  - labels "Axioms" and "Propositions", glyphs **A** and **P**;
+  - the proposition stripe uses the old Goal colour, and green is reserved for proved;
+  - the theme colours become `telelean.kindAxiom`, `telelean.kindProposition` and the new `telelean.proved`. The old `kindAssumption`, `kindDerivation` and `kindGoal` ids are removed, and the theme test's whitelist is updated.
+- **1a:** two columns (Axioms | Propositions); "Make Axiom" on propositions; no "Make Proposition".
+- **1b:**
+  - arrow handles and drawing;
+  - selectable arrows (click; Ctrl adds; Delete removes);
+  - "Select incoming arrows", "Follows from nothing", "Move to axioms", and "Mark pending" (AR-8).
+- **1c:** the canvas and the columns above (§3).
+- **1d:** glows, bands and arrow looks (§4).
+- **1e:** the Context Menu section replaces the tray (CM-1–5): the selection summary, Formalize for dependencies (with disabled reasons), the AR-8 dialog, and the other actions.
+- **1f:** while a run is active, editing UI is disabled with the reason, and Undo/Redo are disabled.
+
+## 3. The canvas (1c)
+
+- **Structure:** a viewport `div` (overflow hidden, focusable) holding one transformed layer (`transform: translate(tx, ty) scale(s)`, via CSS custom properties set from a class; no inline style attributes, because of the CSP: use `element.style.setProperty` from code, which the CSP allows, as EdgeEngine already does with attributes). Cards are absolutely positioned at their layout positions.
+- **Zoom:**
+  - `wheel` with `{ passive: false }`; `s′ = clamp(s · exp(−deltaY · k), 0.1, 4)`, with k larger when `ctrlKey` is set (pinch deltas are small);
+  - keep the point under the cursor fixed: `t′ = c − (c − t) · s′/s`.
+- **Pan:** right-button `pointerdown` → pointer capture → pan.
+- **The right-click menu:**
+  - suppress `contextmenu` on the viewport, the column and the cards (on Linux the event fires on the press);
+  - on right `pointerup`, if the total movement is under 4 px, open the menu (common/Popover) at the pointer, for the thing under it, selecting it first unless it is already selected.
+- **Left-drag:**
+  - on a card: move it (pointer events, not pragmatic-drag-and-drop), committing `move-cards` on release;
+  - released over the AXIOMS column: run the "Move to axioms" flow instead (AR-7, with its confirmation);
+  - an axiom dragged onto the canvas is refused, with the drop text "Draw an arrow into it to make it a proposition";
+  - on empty canvas: a selection rectangle.
+- **Keyboard:**
+  - Tab and Shift+Tab move focus over the cards in order (column, then canvas top-to-bottom, left-to-right), and the canvas follows the focused card;
+  - `+`, `−`, `0` (Fit all), and the arrow keys pan when the viewport has focus.
+- **Toolbar:** Fit all, Zoom to selection, Tidy layout.
+- **Placement:** propositions without a stored position get a layered layout. The x coordinate comes from the longest declared-premise path from a source; the y coordinate stacks cards in file order within a layer, avoiding stored cards. It is computed in the webview, and never written until the user moves the card.
+- **Above the board:**
+  - the Vocabulary and Definitions columns (BD-1), split from `VocabularyGroup`;
+  - a draggable divider, whose height is kept in webview state;
+  - a collapse to one line with counts and flags.
+- **The AXIOMS header** counts presuppositions and hidden assumptions, linking to the Vocabulary column.
+- **EdgeEngine** is generalised from three scrolling lists to the AXIOMS list plus the canvas:
+  - card boxes from `getBoundingClientRect` in board space;
+  - canvas-internal arrows clipped to the viewport;
+  - column ends clamped to the column's visible band, with today's stub badges;
+  - a recompute on scroll, pan, zoom and resize, at most once per frame.
+- **Arrow hit paths:** a transparent wide stroke under each path with `pointer-events: stroke`, for selection and the menu.
+- **Reveal** pans and zooms to the card.
+
+## 4. Glows, bands and arrows (1d)
+
+- **Glows:**
+  - the blue aura (`data-formal='formalized'`) stays;
+  - a new `[data-established]` gives the green glow (`--tl-proved`), which replaces the blue one;
+  - proved but not established keeps blue, plus a chip: "rests on pending: ‹card›", "given: ‹card›" or "uses a hidden assumption";
+  - pending shows "pending proof".
+- **Band:** for each proved or conditional proposition, the verified edges into it form its band.
+  - It is drawn as an arc across the ends of those arrows near the target, in `--tl-proved`, with a "✓" label and the tooltip "Together these suffice (checked by Lean) · consistency unchecked".
+  - A "from nothing" proof draws the band on the ∅ stub.
+  - If the target's statement closure uses definitions, or its footprint has `presup:` entries, the band's tooltip adds "also by definition: …" and "also presupposes: …".
+  - In the proposed view, bands are hidden like verified arrows until the result is revealed (the existing D-19 overlay logic).
+- **Arrow looks** (BD-5):
+  - declared arrows are dotted (`stroke-dasharray` with round caps, e.g. `1 5`);
+  - verified arrows are solid;
+  - conditional arrows keep the hollow head;
+  - TL109 (declared but unused) is no longer drawn in the warning colour: plain dotted, with the tooltip "not used by the current proof";
+  - TL107 (used but undeclared) stays in the warning colour.
+- **Legend:** declared, verified by Lean, conditional, mismatch, formalised, established, band, pending proof.
+- **High contrast:**
+  - the band is an outlined bracket with "✓";
+  - the green glow becomes a 2 px outline in `--tl-proved` with a "✓ established" chip.
+
+## 5. Formalize for dependencies (1e)
+
+- **Selection:** cards, arrows (declared or verified) and ∅ stubs. The tray goes. The Context Menu section in the header shows:
+  - "N arrows into ‹target›";
+  - **Formalize for dependencies**, enabled when the selection contains arrows into exactly one proposition, or that proposition's ∅ stub, and no run is active;
+  - disabled reasons, as CM-3 says;
+  - the other actions for the selection (Select incoming arrows, Follows from nothing, Move to axioms, Delete).
+- **The AR-8 dialog (★D7 (b)):** for each selected source that is a proposition without a `.holds`:
+  - "‹L› is not proved. Mark it pending (assumed until proved), or cancel?";
+  - if L has no Lean statement: "‹L› has no Lean statement and no proof yet: formalize and prove it first", with Cancel only (AP-10).
+- **On confirm:** `startRun(target, sources)`. With only the ∅ stub selected, `premises: []` in the startRun message (today's "Self-evident?" run).
+- **Run panel strings:** "Formalize for dependencies: …" and "Follows from nothing?".
+
+## 6. Tests
